    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143-a1">

                <pb facs="0770" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/pg665"/>


                <head>Memorandum From Burke to McElroy</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-03-02">March 2, 1959</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d143-2" n="2" type="facsimile" xml:id="d143-2"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>U.S. Policy in the Event of War (NSC
                        5904)(C)</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. The Joint Chiefs of Staff have reviewed the draft statement of policy, subject
                    as above, prepared by the NSC Planning Board,
                    for consideration by the NSC at its meeting on
                    Thursday, 5 March 1959.</p>
                <p>2. Subject to the comments contained in Appendix “A” hereto, it is recommended
                    that you concur in the draft of NSC 5904 to
                    supersede NSC 5410/1.</p>
                <p>3. Additional information considered by the Joint Chiefs of Staff to be suitable
                    for your talking purpose, with regard to paragraph 15 on pages 4 and 5 of NSC 5904, is contained in Appendix “B” hereto.</p>
                <p>For the Joint Chiefs of Staff:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">/s/ Arleigh
                            Burke</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Chief of Naval Operations</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
